{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789885016849,"sessionID":"ses_f428a512fffed89OwSRaaEXqP0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_20f1fa6af5de4e8c992d6079","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\README.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Auto Exam Maker — PDF → Interactive Comprehensive Exam Web App\n2: \n3: Upload a PDF (lecture notes, slides, reviewer, textbook). The app hands the PDF to\n4: [opencode](https://opencode.ai) running the **`interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator`**\n5: skill, which builds a complete interactive exam: ~30 questions per chapter,\n6: Timed (10 s/question) / Untimed chapter modes, an always-Untimed Overall Exam,\n7: immediate feedback, real-time scoring, chapter locking, shuffle/reset, an Answer Key,\n8: and an Encyclopedia — all grounded in the uploaded PDF.\n9: \n10: ## How it works\n11: \n12: ```\n13: Browser (index.php upload)\n14:    │  POST api/generate.php\n15:    ▼\n16: PHP saves PDF, creates job id, writes a PowerShell launcher\n17:    │  (detached process)\n18:    ▼\n19: worker.php (CLI) calls:\n20:    opencode run --auto --dir <app> --file <pdf> <prompt using the skill>\n21:    │\n22:    ▼  opencode reads the PDF, loads the skill, writes questions.json\n23: PHP validates the JSON (4 choices, correctAnswer 0..3, explanations)\n24:    ▼\n25: exam.php?id=<id> + assets/exam-app.js render the interactive exam\n26: ```\n27: \n28: Question banks are stored as JSON in `data/exams/<id>/questions.json`; metadata lives\n29: in a SQLite database at `data/exam.db`. Generation runs in the background; the upload\n30: page polls `api/status.php` and opens the exam when ready.\n31: \n32: ## Requirements\n33: \n34: - PHP 8.2+ with `pdo_sqlite` (included by default in XAMPP)\n35: - The `opencode` CLI installed (global npm install)\n36: - Apache running (for the htdocs URL)\n37: \n38: ## Setup\n39: \n40: 1. Put this folder anywhere under `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\`. It is already at\n41:    `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project`.\n42: 2. Make sure your opencode config has a working model/provider (whatever you normally use).\n43: 3. Check `lib/config.php`:\n44:    - `OPENCODE_EXE` — absolute path to `opencode.exe`\n45:      (default: `%APPDATA%\\npm\\node_modules\\opencode-ai\\bin\\opencode.exe`).\n46:    - `PHP_EXE` — absolute path to the CLI PHP (default: `C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe`).\n47:      Override either with the `OPENCODE_EXE` / `PHP_EXE` environment variables.\n48: 4. Start Apache (XAMPP Control → Apache, or `httpd.exe`).\n49: 5. Open **http://localhost/automation/side-project/**.\n50: \n51: The skill itself is bundled in the project at\n52: `.opencode/skills/interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator/SKILL.md` so opencode\n53: auto-discovers it. It is a copy of your `.agents` skill — update it there if you\n54: tune the skill.\n55: \n56: ## Usage\n57: \n58: - **Create**: upload a PDF (≤ 50 MB). Optionally set a title. Watch the status\n59:   spinner; the page auto-opens the exam when done.\n60: - **Take**: chapters → pick **Timed** (10 s/question, timeouts = incorrect) or\n61:   **Untimed** → Start. One question at a time, instant feedback + explanation,\n62:   live score/progress, Shuffle & Reset per chapter.\n63: - **Overall Exam**: combines all chapters, always Untimed, Google Forms style.\n64: - **Answer Key** and **Encyclopedia**: available when no attempt is in progress.\n65: - While a chapter attempt is active, all other sections are locked until you\n66:   finish or reset that chapter.\n67: \n68: ## Notes / limitations\n69: \n70: - **Permissions:** the worker invokes opencode with `--auto` so it can read the\n71:   PDF and write the question bank without interactive prompts. Generation runs\n72:   only on YOUR machine; this is a local tool, not a remote service.\n73: - **Cost/time:** a 7-chapter exam takes roughly 10–15 minutes and produces\n74:   hundreds of questions; plan API usage accordingly. Large or image-heavy PDFs\n75:   increase token use.\n76: - **Accuracy:** the skill treats the PDF as the source of truth. Verify generated\n77:   questions before formal use (an \"Answer Key\" tab exists for quick audit).\n78: - **Job lifecycle:** `queued → running → done | error`. Jobs stuck longer than\n79:   30 minutes are auto-marked `error`.\n80: \n81: ## Project layout\n82: \n83: ```\n84: index.php              upload page + exam list + backend health\n85: exam.php               interactive exam page (fetches the bank via api/data.php)\n86: worker.php             CLI worker that runs opencode with the skill\n87: api/generate.php       upload + spawn detached worker (+ delete op)\n88: api/status.php         job status polling (+ health ping)\n89: api/data.php           validated delivery of a finished question bank\n90: lib/config.php         paths, limits, skill name\n91: lib/db.php             SQLite metadata (exams table)\n92: assets/                site + exam app CSS/JS\n93: data/                  exam.db, job folders, logs (web-inaccessible)\n94: .opencode/skills/      the bundled examiner skill\n95: ```\n\n(End of file - total 95 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Auto Exam Maker — PDF → Interactive Comprehensive Exam Web App\n\nUpload a PDF (lecture notes, slides, reviewer, textbook). The app hands the PDF to\n[opencode](https://opencode.ai) running the **`interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator`**\nskill, which builds a complete interactive exam: ~30 questions per chapter,\nTimed (10 s/question) / Untimed chapter modes, an always-Untimed Overall Exam,\nimmediate feedback, real-time scoring, chapter locking, shuffle/reset, an Answer Key,\nand an Encyclopedia — all grounded in the uploaded PDF.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nBrowser (index.php upload)\n   │  POST api/generate.php\n   ▼\nPHP saves PDF, creates job id, writes a PowerShell launcher\n   │  (detached process)\n   ▼\nworker.php (CLI) calls:\n   opencode run --auto --dir <app> --file <pdf> <prompt using the skill>","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\README.md","text":"# Auto Exam Maker — PDF → Interactive Comprehensive Exam Web App\n\nUpload a PDF (lecture notes, slides, reviewer, textbook). The app hands the PDF to\n[opencode](https://opencode.ai) running the **`interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator`**\nskill, which builds a complete interactive exam: ~30 questions per chapter,\nTimed (10 s/question) / Untimed chapter modes, an always-Untimed Overall Exam,\nimmediate feedback, real-time scoring, chapter locking, shuffle/reset, an Answer Key,\nand an Encyclopedia — all grounded in the uploaded PDF.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nBrowser (index.php upload)\n   │  POST api/generate.php\n   ▼\nPHP saves PDF, creates job id, writes a PowerShell launcher\n   │  (detached process)\n   ▼\nworker.php (CLI) calls:\n   opencode run --auto --dir <app> --file <pdf> <prompt using the skill>\n   │\n   ▼  opencode reads the PDF, loads the skill, writes questions.json\nPHP validates the JSON (4 choices, correctAnswer 0..3, explanations)\n   ▼\nexam.php?id=<id> + assets/exam-app.js render the interactive exam\n```\n\nQuestion banks are stored as JSON in `data/exams/<id>/questions.json`; metadata lives\nin a SQLite database at `data/exam.db`. Generation runs in the background; the upload\npage polls `api/status.php` and opens the exam when ready.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- PHP 8.2+ with `pdo_sqlite` (included by default in XAMPP)\n- The `opencode` CLI installed (global npm install)\n- Apache running (for the htdocs URL)\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Put this folder anywhere under `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\`. It is already at\n   `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project`.\n2. Make sure your opencode config has a working model/provider (whatever you normally use).\n3. Check `lib/config.php`:\n   - `OPENCODE_EXE` — absolute path to `opencode.exe`\n     (default: `%APPDATA%\\npm\\node_modules\\opencode-ai\\bin\\opencode.exe`).\n   - `PHP_EXE` — absolute path to the CLI PHP (default: `C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe`).\n     Override either with the `OPENCODE_EXE` / `PHP_EXE` environment variables.\n4. Start Apache (XAMPP Control → Apache, or `httpd.exe`).\n5. Open **http://localhost/automation/side-project/**.\n\nThe skill itself is bundled in the project at\n`.opencode/skills/interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator/SKILL.md` so opencode\nauto-discovers it. It is a copy of your `.agents` skill — update it there if you\ntune the skill.\n\n## Usage\n\n- **Create**: upload a PDF (≤ 50 MB). Optionally set a title. Watch the status\n  spinner; the page auto-opens the exam when done.\n- **Take**: chapters → pick **Timed** (10 s/question, timeouts = incorrect) or\n  **Untimed** → Start. One question at a time, instant feedback + explanation,\n  live score/progress, Shuffle & Reset per chapter.\n- **Overall Exam**: combines all chapters, always Untimed, Google Forms style.\n- **Answer Key** and **Encyclopedia**: available when no attempt is in progress.\n- While a chapter attempt is active, all other sections are locked until you\n  finish or reset that chapter.\n\n## Notes / limitations\n\n- **Permissions:** the worker invokes opencode with `--auto` so it can read the\n  PDF and write the question bank without interactive prompts. Generation runs\n  only on YOUR machine; this is a local tool, not a remote service.\n- **Cost/time:** a 7-chapter exam takes roughly 10–15 minutes and produces\n  hundreds of questions; plan API usage accordingly. Large or image-heavy PDFs\n  increase token use.\n- **Accuracy:** the skill treats the PDF as the source of truth. Verify generated\n  questions before formal use (an \"Answer Key\" tab exists for quick audit).\n- **Job lifecycle:** `queued → running → done | error`. Jobs stuck longer than\n  30 minutes are auto-marked `error`.\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\nindex.php              upload page + exam list + backend health\nexam.php               interactive exam page (fetches the bank via api/data.php)\nworker.php             CLI worker that runs opencode with the skill\napi/generate.php       upload + spawn detached worker (+ delete op)\napi/status.php         job status polling (+ health ping)\napi/data.php           validated delivery of a finished question bank\nlib/config.php         paths, limits, skill name\nlib/db.php             SQLite metadata (exams table)\nassets/                site + exam app CSS/JS\ndata/                  exam.db, job folders, logs (web-inaccessible)\n.opencode/skills/      the bundled examiner skill\n```","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":95,"totalLines":95,"truncated":false}},"title":"xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\README.md","time":{"start":1789885016644,"end":1789885016838}},"id":"prt_0bd75e9a8001ST8EspyzsmG1TV","sessionID":"ses_f428a512fffed89OwSRaaEXqP0","messageID":"msg_0bd75d65a001GKiPoP78gAKFsD"}}
