{"type":"text","timestamp":1789885765649,"sessionID":"ses_f428a512fffed89OwSRaaEXqP0","part":{"id":"prt_0bd812832001zHlTI7o0F9h2o7","messageID":"msg_0bd80998f001jrdDYWxm4hBcgy","sessionID":"ses_f428a512fffed89OwSRaaEXqP0","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Generate the interactive comprehensive exam for web app job `29l6wh2f5izows` in `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project`: a single valid `questions.json` grounded in the 5-lesson Linux `source.txt`, using the `interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator` skill.\n- The JSON is written and answer positions are balanced; answer-length parity violations still need to be fixed and the exam finalized.\n\n## Important Details\n- Deliverable: `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\29l6wh2f5izows\\questions.json` only — no HTML/CSS/JS/other files.\n- Required schema (what the app/`worker.php` consumes): `title`, `subject`, `summary`, `chapters[{chapterId,title,description,questions[{id,question,choices[4],correctAnswer(0-3),explanation}]}]`, `encyclopedia[{chapterId,term,definition}]`.\n- Source material: `data\\exams\\29l6wh2f5izows\\source.txt` (Lesson 1 System Administration Linux, Lesson 2 File System, Lesson 3 Linux Distributions, Lesson 4 DEs/Package Mgmt/Boot Loaders, Lesson 5 Basic Commands).\n- Question counts: ch1=30, ch2=30, ch3=20, ch4=30, ch5=30 (140 total); ch3 kept small because the source material is thin (distribution list + 4 abbreviations).\n- Answer positions rebalanced via `rebalance.php`: per-chapter targets ch1 `[8,7,8,7]`, ch2 `[8,7,7,8]`, ch3 `[5,5,5,5]`, ch4 `[7,8,7,8]`, ch5 `[7,8,7,8]`; result overall A=35, B=35, C=34, D=36; every chapter spread ≤1.\n- Remaining defect: correct answer is the longest choice in 69/140 (49.3%) — violates answer parity; corrections in progress.\n- PHP available: `C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe` (PHP 8.2.12); helper scripts live in `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\`.\n- `api\\data.php` serves the bank only when `status.json` == `done`; currently `status.json` still says `\"running\"`.\n- Rebalance technique in `rebalance.php`: for each question, splice the choice at old `correctAnswer` index and insert at the new target index.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Loaded skill `interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator`.\n- Explored app pipeline: `worker.php`, `lib/db.php`, `lib/config.php`, `api/data.php`, `api/generate.php`, `api/status.php`, `assets/exam-app.js`, existing `questions.json` examples (e.g., `enaxqoqxb74s4g`).\n- Read `source.txt` and authored the full 140-question bank + encyclopedia (≥10 entries) into `questions.json`.\n- Validated JSON (valid) with `audit.php`; found answer distribution heavily skewed to A (A:78/B:38/C:21/D:3).\n- Wrote and ran `rebalance.php`; re-audited: VALID JSON, balanced letters, but `Correct-answer-longest: 69 / 140 (49.3%)`.\n- Wrote `len_audit.php` and ran it; it flagged length outliers (output truncated at ch1-q25, so more flags may exist later in the file).\n- Applied first parity edit: `ch1-q04` — choices now `Fewer games and software` / `No hardware customization` / `Steep learning curve of commands` / `Frequent virus attacks` (correctAnswer stays 3).\n\n### Active\n- Fixing answer-length parity for remaining flagged questions (exact planned replacement texts for known flags):\n  - `ch1-q08`: shorten correct (currently \"Updates everything at once and never restarts without permission\") to \"Updates everything at once; never restarts without permission\".\n  - `ch1-q09`: leave as-is (A/B are mirrored, equal length — acceptable).\n  - `ch1-q10`: correct → \"Searching Google to find software programs\" (index 3).\n  - `ch1-q11`: correct → \"Connect user applications with the hardware\" (index 2).\n  - `ch1-q15`: choices → \"Embedded kernel model\"/\"Monolithic kernel model\"/\"VM Kernel or Hypervisor\"/\"Hybrid kernel design\" (correct index 2).\n  - `ch1-q24`: correct → \"Initial RAM File System (initramfs)\" (index 2).\n  - `ch1-q25`: correct → \"B